# Sentra Console — environment contract.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) to override. Every value here is a
# PLACEHOLDER; no real credential belongs in this file or in the repository.

# Serve data from MSW fixtures instead of the network.
# No fallback: unset means mocks are OFF, even under `vite dev`
# (src/main.ts:28 checks this value only, never import.meta.env.DEV,
# because the federated E2E suite drives this app against a preview build,
# where DEV is false). Must be set explicitly, here or in `.env.local`.
#
# For the console this is closer to required than optional: M4 ships no real
# ops backend, so a mock-free build has nothing to talk to at all.
VITE_SENTRA_MOCKS=true

# --- Ops backend: deliberately NOT configured here ---------------------------
#
# There is no VITE_SENTRA_OPS_URL or ops token variable, and adding one would be
# scaffolding for a system that does not exist. The client is built from the
# mock service's base URL and a fixed placeholder token — see src/ops.ts:30-40,
# which records that decision. Point the console at a real backend by changing
# createConsoleOpsClient(), not by inventing an environment variable.

# --- Feature-flag overrides: gated on the build mode, not on a variable -------
#
# @sentra/flags can read local overrides from `?ff_<key>=0|1` and from
# localStorage, but only when `allowOverrides` is true. Both call sites
# (src/main.ts:137 and src/federated/register.ts:45) pass
# `import.meta.env.DEV`, which Vite sets from the build mode — it is not a
# variable you set in this file, and setting one here would not enable it.
#
# SECURITY (named risk area: access control). That gate is why no variable is
# offered. Shipped enabled, any visitor who can edit their own URL or
# localStorage could flip any flag on themselves, and a crafted link could do it
# to anyone who opens it. packages/flags/src/overrides.ts:41-58 returns `{}`
# BEFORE reading either source when the gate is false, so a production build
# never consults them at all.
